## Summary

    Completed a hands-on lab focused on identifying malicious activity through network monitoring, malware analysis, and threat intelligence validation. I used Wireshark and tcpdump to capture and analyze network traffic, leveraged Windows Sandbox to safely execute and observe a suspicious file, and utilized WHOIS, AbuseIPDB, and VirusTotal to investigate domains, IP addresses, and URLs. The lab reinforced the importance of packet analysis, secure malware testing, and threat intelligence correlation when identifying indicators of compromise and investigating potentially malicious activity.
